      "content": "That's an interesting suggestion, but the team is leaning towards a clean slate. They're worried that attempting to \"patch\" or \"augment\" the old checkpoint with snapshots from an unstable session might just carry over the same erratic behaviors we're trying to clear out. The directive is to stick to the v4.2 baseline to ensure the results are reproducible and untainted.\n\nDo you see any reason why a purely clean reset would be problematic for the ongoing math proofs?",
